Privacy Policy for Fuel Tracker

Last updated: [date]

Fuel Tracker ("the app") is designed with your privacy in mind.

DATA COLLECTION
The app does not collect, transmit, or share any personal data. All information you enter — vehicle details, fuel entries, costs, odometer readings, and maintenance records — is stored locally on your device only, in a file within the app's private storage area.

NO ACCOUNT, NO CLOUD, NO TRACKING
- The app does not require account creation or sign-in.
- The app does not use any analytics, advertising, or third-party tracking services.
- No data is sent to any server operated by us.

NETWORK ACCESS
The app makes a single outbound request to Apple's public App Store lookup service to check whether a newer version is available. This request contains only the app's bundle identifier — no personal or usage data is included or transmitted.

NOTIFICATIONS
If you enable notifications, they are scheduled and delivered locally by iOS to remind you about upcoming or overdue vehicle maintenance. No notification content is sent to or processed by any external server.

DATA DELETION
You can delete all app data at any time from within the app's Settings screen. Uninstalling the app also permanently removes all stored data, since nothing is stored outside your device.

CHILDREN'S PRIVACY
The app is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect any data from anyone, including children, since it collects no data at all.

CHANGES TO THIS POLICY
If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted at this same address with a revised "Last updated" date.

CONTACT
